nvidia-drm: build against Linux 7.x

Local workaround; not ppc64le specific. 7.2 changes that 535.216.03's nvidia-drm does not know:
struct drm_atomic_state is now struct drm_atomic_commit (helpers renamed to match, drm_atomic_state_free()
gone); the per-object .state pointer is .state_to_destroy; conftest.sh probes five signatures with the old
struct name so those verdicts come out negative; <drm/drm_print.h> is no longer pulled in indirectly;
fb_create() and drm_helper_mode_fill_fb_struct() take a const struct drm_format_info *; struct drm_driver has
no .date; dma_fence_signal() returns void; connector mode_valid() returns enum drm_mode_status and takes a
const mode; struct drm_mode_create_dumb is not declared before nv_drm_dumb_create()'s prototype.

All behind NV_DRM_7X_COMPAT (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= 7.2.0) in the new nvidia-drm-7x-compat.h.
Loaded 2026-10-04 on 7.2.9 with modeset=0: registers /dev/dri/card1-4 and four render nodes, no kernel
messages. modeset=1 and any display use are untested (the V100 has no display outputs).

